# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > l+ l- j at LO (default coupling orders).
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The default-order half of the llj pair. One extra QCD coupling for the
#     jet takes the order selection past the trivial case, so this and the
#     QCD=2 QED=2 scripts (pp_to_llj_fixed, pp_to_llj_dyn) together pin what
#     "default orders" means once more than one power of a coupling is in play:
#     the two spellings must select the same diagram content, and a change to
#     the selector that broke that would show up as one count moving.
#   - Its run card takes MadGraph's dynamical scale choice over a 2 -> 3, so
#     every event's SCALUP / <rscale> / <pdfrwt> comes out of the general kT
#     clustering rather than a closed form. validate_scales replays all 10000
#     of them field by field.
#
# Not used for cross sections or event samples: its beams take MadGraph's
# internal nn23lo1 parton densities, which the LHAPDF6 grid reader here cannot
# load. pp_to_llj_fixed and pp_to_llj_dyn card the same generate line onto
# lhaid 247000 and are the integrals, samples and event-generation subjects.
generate p p > l+ l- j
output pp_to_llj -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  done
